what happened to one, three,
four, and five and seven?

00:09:47.210 --> 00:09:49.380
I want to be smart enough as a doctor

00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:51.732
to come up with my own hormone types.

00:09:51.732 --> 00:09:54.482
(rhythmic music)

00:09:55.730 --> 00:09:57.610
You definitely want to sanitize the area

00:09:57.610 --> 00:09:59.630
before you do any kind of micro-needling.

00:09:59.630 --> 00:10:00.593
That's smart.

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:04.460
If you're gonna be making
abrasions in your skin

00:10:04.460 --> 00:10:06.910
so much can go wrong,
especially on the face.

00:10:06.910 --> 00:10:08.970
I just wouldn't trust a random device

00:10:08.970 --> 00:10:09.880
bought off the internet.

00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:12.280
- Kind of felt like getting a tattoo.

00:10:12.280 --> 00:10:15.930
Had only a couple spots that
bled just a teeny tiny bit.

00:10:15.930 --> 00:10:18.690
- People really trust these things.

00:10:18.690 --> 00:10:19.970
Being a family medicine doctor,

00:10:19.970 --> 00:10:21.970
not a plastic surgeon or a dermatologist,

00:10:21.970 --> 00:10:24.500
When a patient comes in
with even a small laceration

00:10:24.500 --> 00:10:25.740
that requires sutures on the face

00:10:25.740 --> 00:10:27.010
I'm always hesitant to do it

00:10:27.010 --> 00:10:28.070
because I want to make sure

00:10:28.070 --> 00:10:30.420
that it's as less scarring
as possible happening.

00:10:30.420 --> 00:10:32.740
So, I let someone with a
lot more experience do it.

00:10:32.740 --> 00:10:34.180
These people are just like,

00:10:34.180 --> 00:10:36.744
doing micro-needling on
themselves with no fear.

00:10:36.744 --> 00:10:38.510
(upbeat music)

00:10:38.510 --> 00:10:40.170
Oh, not ear candling.

00:10:40.170 --> 00:10:43.114
There's a warning from
the FDA to not do this.

00:10:43.114 --> 00:10:45.697
(upbeat music)

00:10:48.510 --> 00:10:51.290
So, this is BS because
this has been tested

00:10:51.290 --> 00:10:53.560
and we actually see no suction happening

00:10:53.560 --> 00:10:54.600
as a result of the flame.

00:10:54.600 --> 00:10:57.990
We also see that that is residue

00:10:57.990 --> 00:11:01.070
of the actual paraffin wax or beeswax

00:11:01.070 --> 00:11:02.960
that is inside this candle thing

00:11:02.960 --> 00:11:06.210
because we see this same
residue on these candles

00:11:06.210 --> 00:11:07.750
that have not been put into ears.

00:11:07.750 --> 00:11:09.300
On top of that, do you know
how many of my colleagues

00:11:09.300 --> 00:11:12.410
have treated burns from
this ear wax nonsense?

00:11:12.410 --> 00:11:13.440
Oh my god!

00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:15.120
- Life-saving advice from movies

00:11:15.120 --> 00:11:16.780
that can actually kill you.

00:11:16.780 --> 00:11:17.870
According to Hollywood,

00:11:17.870 --> 00:11:19.970
if someone has passed out with no pulse,

00:11:19.970 --> 00:11:21.400
you should straddle them,

00:11:21.400 --> 00:11:23.620
give them mouth to mouth
and beat on their chest.

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:24.930
- Yeah, don't beat on people's chest.

00:11:24.930 --> 00:11:26.650
Don't give them mouth to
mouth, if someone's passed out,

00:11:26.650 --> 00:11:27.880
all you have to do is chest compressions,

00:11:27.880 --> 00:11:29.150
chest compressions, chest compressions.

00:11:29.150 --> 00:11:31.040
- I'm not saying CPR doesn't work,

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:33.740
but it only works like two
to four percent of the time

00:11:33.740 --> 00:11:35.160
and when properly performed,

00:11:35.160 --> 00:11:37.800
you usually end up cracking
the person's rib cage.

00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:38.850
- My man is confused here

00:11:38.850 --> 00:11:41.460
because he's saying
pounding on their chest

00:11:41.460 --> 00:11:43.780
versus performing chest
compressions is both CPR.

00:11:43.780 --> 00:11:45.200
Factually untrue.

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:46.800
The purpose of performing CPR

00:11:46.800 --> 00:11:48.296
is not to bring someone
back, it's to buy time

00:11:48.296 --> 00:11:51.220
so other interventions can be done,

00:11:51.220 --> 00:11:53.040
like giving them
medications like epinephrin

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:54.860
or perhaps bringing a defibrillator along

00:11:54.860 --> 00:11:56.800
because the reason you're
pumping on someone's chest

00:11:56.800 --> 00:11:59.210
is to circulate the blood
that's already in their body

00:11:59.210 --> 00:12:01.440
that has some oxygen still left in it

00:12:01.440 --> 00:12:04.040
and the breaking of the ribs, no big deal.

00:12:04.040 --> 00:12:04.873
Why?

00:12:04.873 --> 00:12:06.410
Because the person is already dead.

00:12:06.410 --> 00:12:08.460
So, if you can extend their possibility

00:12:08.460 --> 00:12:10.090
of being brought back to life

00:12:10.090 --> 00:12:13.790
by breaking a rib, fair
trade-off, wouldn't you say?

00:12:13.790 --> 00:12:16.630
